This Ordinance is being adopted for the following general purposes:
A.
Protection & Promotion. To protect and promote the public health, safety, and welfare of the people and community;
B.
Districts. To divide the Town into zones and Districts restricting and regulating therein the location, construction, reconstruction, Alteration, and Use of Buildings, Structures, and land for Residential, Business, Commercial, Industrial, manufacturing, and other specified Uses;
C.
Character & Stability. To protect the character and maintain the stability of and enhance Residential, Business, Commercial, and Industrial areas within the Town's jurisdiction, and to promote the orderly and beneficial development of such areas;
D.
Appropriate Use of Land. To encourage appropriate Uses of land;
E.
Light, Air, Privacy & Access. To provide adequate light, air, privacy, sanitation, and convenience of access to property;
F.
Open Space. To regulate the intensity of Open Spaces surrounding Buildings that are necessary to provide adequate light and air and protect the health;
G.
Building Lines & Locations. To establish Building lines and the location of Buildings designated for Residential, Business, Commercial, Industrial, manufacturing, or other Uses within such lines;
H.
Standards. To fix reasonable standards to which Buildings or Structures shall conform;
I.
Prohibit Incompatible Character & Uses. To prohibit Uses, Buildings, or Structures which are incompatible with the character of Development or the permitted Uses within specified zoning Districts;
J.
Restrict Noncomplying Changes. To restrict such additions to, and alterations or remodeling of, existing Buildings or Structures as would not comply with the restrictions and limitations imposed hereunder;
K.
Congestion, Parking & Loading. To minimize traffic hazards and congestion in the Streets and to protect the public health, safety, convenience, and general welfare by providing for the Parking of vehicles and for the loading and unloading of vehicles;
L.
Protect Against Hazards. To reduce and provide protection against fire, flood, explosion, noxious fumes, and other hazards in the interest of the public health, safety, comfort, and general welfare;
M.
Prevent Overcrowding. To prevent overcrowding of land and undue concentration of Structures and population so far as is possible and appropriate in each District by regulating the Use and bulk of Buildings in relation to the land surrounding them and the form and character of Development;
N.
Preserve Value. To preserve the value of land and Buildings throughout the Town;
O.
Gradually Eliminate Nonconformities. To provide for the gradual elimination of those Uses of land, Buildings and other Structures which do not conform to the standards of the Districts in which they are respectively located and which are adversely affecting the Development and taxable value of property in each District;
P.
Define Powers & Duties. To define and limit the powers and duties of the administrative officers and bodies as provided herein;
Q.
Beneficial Use of Property. To protect and in general allow for the beneficial Uses of property;
R.
Assist with Services. To assist in the economic provision, utilization, and expansion of services and to provide for the public when determined desirable and appropriate, including, but not limited to, police, fire, and public works, and recreation services, and to make arrangements with third parties to provide water, sewer, communications, and solid waste services; and
S.
Protection & Enhancement of Amenities. To protect and where appropriate, enhance the natural, man-made, and historical amenities of the Town.

A.
Residential. Where the phrase "Residential District" or Residentially-zoned" is used in this Ordinance, the phrase shall be construed to include the following Districts:
1.
Character District CD-2L (Rural - Large);
2.
Character District CD-2 (Rural);
3.
Character District CD-3L (Neighborhood - Large);
4.
Character District CD-3 (Neighborhood);
5.
Any portion of Character District CD-4 (Neighborhood Center) used or available for Residential Use;
6.
Any portion of Character District CD-4C (Neighborhood Corridor) used or available for Residential Use;
7.
Any portion of Character District CD-4HV (Historic Village) used or available for Residential Use;
8.
Any portion of Character District CD-RH (Residential Hamlet) used or available for Residential Use;
9.
Any portion of Character District CD-CH (Commercial Hamlet) used or available for Residential Use;
10.
Any portion of an existing Planned Unit Development or Planned Development District used or available for Residential Use.
B.
Commercial. Where the phrase "Commercial District" or "Commercially-zoned" is used in this Ordinance, the phrase shall be construed to include the following Districts:
1.
Any portion of Character District CD-4 (Neighborhood Center) used or available for Commercial Use;
2.
Any portion of Character District CD-4C (Neighborhood Corridor) used or available for Commercial Use;
3.
Any portion of Character District CD-4HV (Historic Village) used or available for Commercial Use;
4.
Any portion of Character District CD-RH (Residential Hamlet) used or available for Commercial Use;
5.
Any portion of Character District CD-CH (Commercial Hamlet) used or available for Commercial Use;
6.
Any portion of Character District CD-OI (Office Industrial) used or available for Commercial Use; and
7.
Any portion of an existing Planned Unit Development or used or available for Commercial Use.
C.
Industrial. Where the phrase "Industrial District" or "Industrially-zoned" is used in this Ordinance, the phrase shall be construed to include the following districts:
1.
Character District CD-OI (Office Industrial); and
2.
Any portion of an existing Planned Unit Development District or Planned Development District used or available for Industrial Use.
D.
Non-Residential. Where the phrase "Non-residential District" is used in this Ordinance, the phrase shall be construed to include any of the Districts or portions thereof listed in Sections 3.7.2.B and 3.7.2.C.

Except as otherwise provided in Section 1.22 with respect to Nonconformities, none of the following shall occur with respect to any project or proposal involving a Development Parcel, except in compliance with this Article 5, the Official Zoning Map, and pursuant to a Development Plan that conforms with and has been prepared, submitted, reviewed and approved in accordance with Section 8.5.6, this Article 5, and all other standards and requirements applicable thereto:
A.
Construction Activities. Construction, re-construction, Alteration, modification, raising, moving, extending, reducing, or enlarging any Structure;
B.
Development Activities. Development, re-Development, Improvement, subdivision, or re-subdivision of any Lot, Building Site, or other parcel of land;
C.
Use. Use of any Structure, Lot, Building Site, or other parcel of land;
D.
Applications and Actions.
1.
Filing, issuing, applying for, certifying, or approving any subdivision application or plat, Building Permit, Development Plan or other Zoning Permit, relating to, or subdividing, re-subdividing, commencing Construction on, or Developing, or Improving any part of a Development Parcel;
2.
Approving any Zoning Map or Zoning Map amendment, other than any Zoning Map or Zoning Map Amendment prepared by or on behalf of the Town.

The following Tree Removal activities are exempt from this Section 6.8:
1.
The tree proposed for removal is located:
a.
on a Single-Family Detached Residential Lot or Building Site of one (1) acre or less; or
2.
Removal of trees that are determined to be unhealthy by the Zoning Administrator or with written verification of the tree's condition as dead, dying, or structurally unsound as prepared by a certified arborist;
3.
Removal of trees that are determined by the Zoning Administrator to be nuisance trees or a threat to an existing Structure, underground Utility, or public safety;
4.
Removal of trees that encroach into established utility easements;
5.
Removal of trees that will result in damage to utilities or Structures from tree roots;
6.
Removal of trees listed in the current edition of Invasive Exotic Pest Plants, published by the Tennessee Exotic Pest Plant Council;
7.
Removal of trees on Town-owned land or within public right-of-way by the Town or its authorized agent;
8.
Removal of a tree is necessary to access the site and no alternative exists for relocating such access, as determined by the Zoning Administrator;
9.
The Zoning Administrator makes an exception for removal of a tree or trees in extraordinary circumstances, such as weather-related emergencies, natural disasters, or similar occurrences.

Development review as regulated by this Ordinance, may involve one or more of the following types of Applications, requests, and Development reviews:
1.
Interpretation of this Ordinance;
2.
Building Permit;
3.
Sketch Development Plan Review;
4.
Site Development Plan Review;
5.
Administrative Adjustment;
6.
Temporary Use Permit;
7.
Home Occupation Permit;
8.
Certificate of Occupancy;
9.
Historic District Designation;
10.
Certificate of Appropriateness;
11.
Demolition by Neglect;
12.
Certificate of Economic Hardship;
13.
Conditional Use Permit;
14.
Variance;
15.
Appeal of Administrative Decision;
16.
Zoning Ordinance Amendment;
17.
Rezoning;
18.
Comprehensive Plan, Major Thoroughfare Plan, or other Land Use Plan Amendment or Adoption;
19.
Sign Permit;
20.
Other Applications and Reviews.
